{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"tpk-autorun-fix","name":"TPK autorun fix","version":"0.4.0","apiVersion":1,"description":"Reopens the last app at power-on when Samsung's Autorun Last App skips it (.tpk apps you installed yourself).","author":"Namer03","permissions":["exec"],"main":"index.js"},"files":{"README.md":"# TPK autorun fix\n\nSamsung's **Autorun Last App** brings web apps (.wgt) and Samsung's own apps back when the TV wakes up, but not\n.tpk apps you installed yourself. With this Shard on, the app you were using comes back too.\n\nWhile the TV is on, it notes which of your own .tpk apps is on screen. When the TV goes to sleep with one on screen,\nit opens that app again as soon as the TV wakes up. Everything else is left to Samsung.\n\n## How it decides\n\n- **Watched apps:** apps whose package is a `.tpk` and removable (installed by you), except `com.samsung.*` and\n  `org.tizen.*`. Samsung's own apps and all web apps (.wgt) are left to Samsung. Each app is checked once, the first\n  time it is on screen.\n- **Armed at sleep:** the watched app that was on screen last, more recently than any other app. Samsung hides the\n  app a moment before the TV reports sleep; samples with nothing on screen do not change the choice.\n- **At wake:** it launches the app at once and stops when the app has been on screen for two samples. If Samsung covers\n  it, it tries again, at most 3 launches within 20 s.\n- **Never over something else:** if anything other than Samsung Home or the source viewer is on screen at wake (an app\n  you opened, Ambient mode), it does not launch, and it stops retrying the moment you open another app.\n- **After a full restart** (long press on power, power cut): if Vetro starts within 5 minutes of the TV booting and an\n  app was armed, that counts as a wake-up.\n\n## Permissions\n\n`exec`: reading the TV's power state, which apps are on screen and the installed package files needs the root agent,\nand so does opening an app.\n\n## Commands it runs\n\n| Command | When | Why |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `vconftool get memory/pm/state` | every second | 1 = TV on, 4 = asleep |\n| `aul_test getallappstatus` | every second, only while the TV is on | which apps are visible (status 3) |\n| `grep` on `/opt/share/packages/<package>.xml` | once per app seen on screen | is it a .tpk you installed |\n| `/usr/bin/app_launcher -s <app>` | at wake, only for the armed app | open it again |\n\nApp and package names are checked against `[A-Za-z0-9_.-]` before they are put in a command.\nWhile the TV sleeps only the first command runs. It does not change any setting.\n\n## Network\n\nNone.\n\n## Data it keeps\n\n`ctx.config` (its own `config.json`): the armed app, the time of the last sleep and of the last launch.\nThe dashboard status shows the TV state, the app on screen, the armed app, the watched apps and the last 15 events\n(with the apps seen in the last 3 samples before each sleep).\n\n## Tested on\n\nSamsung S95C (QE65S95CATXXH), Tizen 9.0: sleep and wake with Nuvio Legacy (.NET .tpk) on screen; it came back on\nthe first launch, within about a second of the TV waking. A web app (Stremio) on screen was left to Samsung.\nOther models and Tizen versions are not tested: if `memory/pm/state` reads differently there, the Shard does nothing\nand shows the error in its status. Not tested with HDMI-CEC wake (a console turning the TV on) or Ambient mode.\n\n## Samsung's Autorun Last App setting\n\nThe Shard does not follow it: the setting is not stored where the Shard can read it (no settings key changes when it\nis toggled). To stop the Shard, switch it off in Vetro Shards.\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// TPK autorun fix: Samsung's \"Autorun Last App\" brings back web apps (.wgt) and native apps, but not\n// user-installed .tpk apps (measured on the S95C, Tizen 9: the TV never resumes them at power-on).\n// This Shard does it instead: while the TV is on it notes which such app is on screen; when the TV goes\n// to sleep with one on screen, it launches that app again at the next power-on.\n// Plain ES5: the TV may run Node 4.4.\n//\n// Signals (measured on the S95C):\n//   memory/pm/state = 1 while the TV is on, 4 while it sleeps (Vetro keeps running in standby).\n//   aul_test getallappstatus: status 3 = visible.\n//   /opt/share/packages/<pkgid>.xml: the installed package, with its app type and removable flag.\n\nvar os = require('os');\n\nvar POLL_MS = 1000;            // how often the TV is sampled\nvar FIRST_LAUNCH_MS = 0;       // launch as soon as power-on is seen\nvar CHECK_MS = 2000;           // after a launch, look again this long later\nvar MAX_LAUNCHES = 3;          // launches per power-on, at most\nvar WINDOW_MS = 20000;         // stop trying this long after power-on\nvar BOOT_UPTIME_S = 300;       // Vetro starting this soon after a TV boot counts as a power-on\nvar LOG_MAX = 15;\n\nvar ID_RE = /^[A-Za-z0-9_.-]{1,120}$/;\nvar STATE_RE = /value = (-?\\d+)/;\n// Samsung's own apps and the platform's: Samsung decides about these itself.\nvar SYSTEM_RE = /^(com\\.samsung\\.|org\\.tizen\\.|com\\.samsung$)/;\n// What Samsung itself puts on screen at power-on (measured on the S95C): Samsung Home, the source viewer.\n// Anything else visible during the retries was opened by the person.\nvar WAKE_SCREEN_RE = /^(com\\.samsung\\.tv\\.csfs|org\\.tizen\\.tv-viewer)$/;\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var timer = null, busy = false, stopped = true;\n    var cfg = {};\n    var tvOn = null;                // null until the first sample\n    var lastOnSample = null;        // {app: appId or null, at: ms} from the last sample with the TV on\n    // Pressing power hides the app (focus lost, paused) while the TV still reports \"on\" for a moment,\n    // so the very last sample can show nothing. What counts is the last app really seen on screen.\n    var lastWatched = null;         // {app, at}: a watched app seen visible\n    var lastOther = null;           // {app, at}: any other app seen visible (home, Sources, ...)\n    var recent = [];                // the last 3 samples' visible apps, logged at sleep\n    var wake = null;                // {app, at, launches, nextAt, seen} while a power-on is being handled\n    var kinds = {};                 // appId -> true (a .tpk the user installed) / false\n    var log = [];\n    var lastError = null;\n\n    function now() { return Date.now(); }\n    // The TV's local time, as the person reads it on screen.\n    function stamp() {\n        var d = new Date();\n        function two(n) { return (n < 10 ? '0' : '') + n; }\n        return d.getFullYear() + '-' + two(d.getMonth() + 1) + '-' + two(d.getDate()) + ' ' +\n            two(d.getHours()) + ':' + two(d.getMinutes()) + ':' + two(d.getSeconds());\n    }\n    function note(text) {\n        log.unshift(stamp() + ' ' + text);\n        if (log.length > LOG_MAX) log.length = LOG_MAX;\n    }\n    function save(patch) {\n        var k;\n        for (k in patch) if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(patch, k)) cfg[k] = patch[k];\n        try { ctx.config.set(cfg); } catch (e) { lastError = 'config: ' + e.message; }\n    }\n    function text(r) { return (r && (r.stdout || r.output)) || ''; }\n\n    function sample() {\n        var cmd = 's=$(vconftool get memory/pm/state 2>&1); echo \"S $s\"; ' +\n            'case \"$s\" in *\"value = 1 \"*) aul_test getallappstatus 2>&1 | ' +\n            'awk \\'/appid:/{a=$2} /pkgid:/{p=$2} /status: 3[[:space:]]*$/{print \"V \" a \" \" p}\\';; esac';\n        return ctx.execute(cmd, 15000).then(function (r) {\n            var out = text(r);\n            var m = STATE_RE.exec(out);\n            if (!m) throw new Error('power state unreadable: ' + out.slice(0, 120));\n            var visible = [];\n            out.split('\\n').forEach(function (line) {\n                var f = line.split(/\\s+/);\n                if (f[0] === 'V' && ID_RE.test(f[1] || '') && ID_RE.test(f[2] || '')) visible.push({ app: f[1], pkg: f[2] });\n            });\n            return { state: +m[1], visible: visible };\n        });\n    }\n\n    // Is this an app Samsung skips: a .tpk package installed by the user (removable)? Read once per app.\n    function classify(v) {\n        if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(kinds, v.app)) return Promise.resolve();\n        if (SYSTEM_RE.test(v.app)) { kinds[v.app] = false; return Promise.resolve(); }\n        var f = '/opt/share/packages/' + v.pkg + '.xml';\n        var cmd = 'f=' + f + '; [ -f \"$f\" ] && grep -q \\'removable=\"true\"\\' \"$f\" && grep -q \\'type=\"tpk\"\\' \"$f\" && echo YES || echo NO';\n        return ctx.execute(cmd, 10000).then(function (r) {\n            kinds[v.app] = text(r).indexOf('YES') >= 0;\n            if (kinds[v.app]) note('watching ' + v.app + ' (user-installed .tpk)');\n        });\n    }\n    function classifyAll(s) {\n        var chain = Promise.resolve();\n        s.visible.forEach(function (v) { chain = chain.then(function () { return classify(v); }); });\n        return chain.then(function () { return s; });\n    }\n\n    function launch(reason) {\n        wake.launches++;\n        note('launch ' + wake.app + ' (' + reason + ', try ' + wake.launches + ')');\n        save({ lastLaunch: stamp() + ' ' + wake.app });\n        return ctx.execute('/usr/bin/app_launcher -s ' + wake.app + ' 2>&1', 15000).then(function (r) {\n            var out = text(r).replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n            note('app_launcher: ' + (out.slice(0, 100) || 'exit ' + (r && r.exit_code)));\n        });\n    }\n\n    function endWake(why) {\n        note('power-on handled: ' + why);\n        wake = null;\n        save({ armedApp: null });\n    }\n    function startWake(t, app) {\n        wake = { app: app, at: t, launches: 0, nextAt: t + FIRST_LAUNCH_MS, seen: 0 };\n    }\n\n    function handle(s) {\n        // A sample that was already on its way when the Shard was switched off does nothing.\n        if (stopped) return null;\n        var on = s.state === 1;\n        var t = now();\n        var shown = null, i;\n        for (i = 0; i < s.visible.length; i++) if (kinds[s.visible[i].app]) { shown = s.visible[i].app; break; }\n        var armed = typeof cfg.armedApp === 'string' && ID_RE.test(cfg.armedApp) ? cfg.armedApp : null;\n\n        if (tvOn === null) {\n            // First sample since this Shard started. A TV that just booted with an app still armed\n            // was switched off (or lost power) with that app on screen.\n            tvOn = on;\n            note('started: TV ' + (on ? 'on' : 'asleep (state ' + s.state + ')') + (armed ? ', armed for ' + armed : ''));\n            if (on && armed && os.uptime() < BOOT_UPTIME_S) {\n                startWake(t, armed);\n                note('TV booted recently: treating this as a power-on');\n            }\n        } else if (tvOn && !on) {\n            tvOn = false;\n            var last = lastWatched && (!lastOther || lastWatched.at >= lastOther.at) ? lastWatched.app : null;\n            wake = null;\n            save({ armedApp: last, offAt: stamp() });\n            note('last samples before sleep (newest first): ' + recent.join(' | '));\n            note('TV asleep (state ' + s.state + '); ' + (last ? last + ' was the last app on screen: armed' :\n                'last app on screen: ' + (lastOther ? lastOther.app : 'none seen')));\n        } else if (!tvOn && on) {\n            tvOn = true;\n            note('TV on' + (armed ? ': ' + armed + ' was last, relaunching' : ''));\n            if (armed) startWake(t, armed);\n        }\n\n        if (on) {\n            lastOnSample = { app: shown, at: t };\n            var others = s.visible.filter(function (v) { return !kinds[v.app]; }).map(function (v) { return v.app; });\n            if (shown) lastWatched = { app: shown, at: t };\n            else if (others.length) lastOther = { app: others[0], at: t };\n            recent.unshift(s.visible.length ? s.visible.map(function (v) { return v.app; }).join(',') : '(none)');\n            if (recent.length > 3) recent.length = 3;\n        }\n\n        if (!wake || !on) return null;\n        var back = s.visible.some(function (v) { return v.app === wake.app; });\n        // Done once the app stays on screen for two samples in a row (Samsung covered one once ~3 s in).\n        if (back && wake.launches > 0) {\n            wake.seen++;\n            if (wake.seen >= 2) endWake(wake.app + ' is on screen');\n            return null;\n        }\n        wake.seen = 0;\n        // Anything other than Samsung's own power-on screens is on screen: the person opened something, or the TV\n        // woke into something else (an input, Ambient mode). Never launch over it, and never pull anyone back.\n        var other = s.visible.filter(function (v) { return v.app !== wake.app && !WAKE_SCREEN_RE.test(v.app); })[0];\n        if (other) {\n            endWake(other.app + ' is on screen: ' + (wake.launches ? 'not retrying' : 'not launching'));\n            return null;\n        }\n        if (t - wake.at > WINDOW_MS) { endWake('gave up after ' + wake.launches + ' launch(es)'); return null; }\n        if (t < wake.nextAt) return null;\n        if (wake.launches >= MAX_LAUNCHES) return null; // wait for the window to close or the app to appear\n        wake.nextAt = t + CHECK_MS;\n        return launch(wake.launches ? 'still not on screen' : 'power-on');\n    }\n\n    function tick() {\n        if (stopped || busy) return;\n        busy = true;\n        sample().then(classifyAll).then(handle).then(function () {\n            lastError = null;\n        }).catch(function (e) {\n            lastError = e && e.message ? e.message : String(e);\n        }).then(function () {\n            busy = false;\n        });\n    }\n\n    return {\n        start: function () {\n            cfg = ctx.config.get() || {};\n            stopped = false; tvOn = null; lastOnSample = null; wake = null; busy = false;\n            lastWatched = null; lastOther = null; recent = [];\n            timer = setInterval(tick, POLL_MS);\n            tick();\n        },\n        stop: function () {\n            stopped = true;\n            if (timer) clearInterval(timer);\n            timer = null;\n        },\n        status: function () {\n            return {\n                tv: tvOn === null ? 'unknown' : tvOn ? 'on' : 'asleep',\n                onScreen: lastOnSample && lastOnSample.app || null,\n                armedFor: cfg.armedApp || null,\n                lastLaunch: cfg.lastLaunch || null,\n                watched: Object.keys(kinds).filter(function (k) { return kinds[k]; }),\n                error: lastError,\n                log: log\n            };\n        },\n        route: function () { return false; }\n    };\n};\n"}}
